        "parms": "# funbuff — a function as points\nA funbuff stores (x, y) pairs of ints, kept sorted by x. Send it an x and it sends the y stored there or, when there is none, the y at the nearest lower x: the function is a staircase. A number on the right inlet waits for the next x, which then stores the pair instead. This one holds (0, 10), (100, 50) and (300, 20). It was sent embed 1, so they are saved with the patch.\nUnlike Max, a funbuff does not read or write files and has no editing window.",
